## Definition of “Full Prototype”
A release qualifies when all **P0 items (§24)** and the core **P1 credibility items** in [DOCS/specsheet(2).md](DOCS/specsheet(2).md#L862-L901) are implemented, verified, and evidenced. Specifically:
1. Security/authorization hardening completed and auditable.
2. Source timestamps govern ingestion and temporal logic, with immutable raw telemetry and provenance-preserving self-healing.
3. Assessments expose quality, severity, classification, readiness, evidence completeness, peer evidence, and root cause (with regional-event safeguards).
4. Evidence API/UI, demo replay, and historical seeding are production-ready.
5. Drift monitoring, fusion calibration status, maintenance persistence, and operator workflows reach P1 credibility.
6. Demo scenarios A (sensor fault) and B (regional weather) are reproducible via deterministic replay.
7. Acceptance dossier maps every requirement to tests, screenshots/logs, or demo steps; `project_acceptance.status` becomes "PASS".

